# Never descend into the OrbStack NFS mount (KI-13).
# ~/OrbStack is an NFS share served by OrbStack Helper: a $HOME-rooted walk turns
# every directory entry into an RPC across every image layer of every container.
# An explicit --glob is NOT neutralised by --no-ignore/-u, which makes this the rg
# analogue of fd's --one-file-system. Unanchored form: a leading / would anchor to
# the search root, not the filesystem root (silent placebo).
--glob=!OrbStack/

# Never print secret stores. Resolved secret files (*.resolved.sh: references
# injected with their real values), *.secured* / *.secret* / *.s3k* stores hold
# credentials in clear: a broad `rg` from a dotfiles root once printed API keys
# from them into a session transcript. Same reason as above for --glob: it holds
# under --no-ignore/-u; `rg --no-config` is the deliberate way around it.
--glob=!*.resolved.sh
--glob=!*.secured*
--glob=!*.secret*
--glob=!*.s3k*
